# This project is handed over as a folder (a zip). This file is for keeping the code in a
# private git repository: it leaves out what is machine-specific, what the pipeline makes
# again by itself, what is too large or may not be redistributed, and every video or image of
# real people. What stays versioned: the code, the READMEs, the camera calibration, the lock
# files, the trained NeRF and the viewer's arena layers.

# --- Python environments and caches (uv creates the environments on the first run)
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Node (the viewer)
node_modules/
src/viewer/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# --- Editors and operating systems
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- The input videos: large, and they show real people
input_videos/*
!input_videos/README.md
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv

# --- Everything the pipeline writes while it runs
work/
*.log
*.tmp
*.tmp.*

# --- Results the pipeline writes into the viewer (made again by `uv run pipeline.py`)
src/viewer/public/bodies/
src/viewer/public/bodies.json
src/viewer/public/people_thumbs/
src/viewer/public/nerf/
src/viewer/public/*.bak.json
src/people/crops/
src/people/3D_People/out/

# --- Model files. SMPL-X may not be redistributed and the OSNet weights are large; the READMEs
#     say where they come from. The trained NeRF (NeRF/model/nerf.pt) is small and stays.
src/people/models/
src/people/3D_People/models/
*.pth
*.npz
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.zip

# --- Frames, crops and thumbnails show real people and are never published. The zip carries
#     the viewer's camera thumbnails (public/thumbs/) and the Annotate tab's frames (public/gt_frames/).
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png

# --- Point clouds are large. Two sets stay: the NeRF floor (NeRF/model/) and the arena layers
#     of the viewer's 3D tab (public/plys/, about 100 MB), which nothing regenerates.
*.ply
!NeRF/model/*.ply
!src/viewer/public/plys/*.ply
